    title: "auto-pr: force-push after rebase creates new CI run that blocks merge"  # d3ba
    status: todo_hard  # d3ba
    priority: 2  # d3ba
    parent:  # d3ba
    tags:  # d3ba
    - ci_infrastructure  # d3ba
    before: []  # d3ba
    duplicate_of: []  # d3ba
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d3ba
    pr_ref:  # d3ba
    description: "When auto-pr rebases and force-pushes, the new commit SHA triggers a fresh CI run. If a tracker auto-sync also merges around the same time, its pending statuses can block the real PR. Observed with PR #1774: original SHA 53de7318 passed CI, but rebase produced 95ccf0e3 which triggered new CI run 4615 that never completed, blocking merge. The tracker sync PR also triggered ci.yml (not just tracker-ci.yml) because the commit contained both ops and code files. Root cause: rebased commits lose their CI status, and concurrent tracker syncs can interfere."  # d3ba
    fields: {}  # d3ba
